 CellLabel->"Out[7]= ",ExpressionUUID->"04d3fcbf-45ed-462a-bda3-94f2760ec31f"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The consequence is exactly what the theory predicts: the quotient is ",
 StyleBox["not", "TI"],
 " quasi-isomorphic to the model. It is three-dimensional with zero \
differential: the cohomology of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["CP",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "876c1351-015c-4466-abec-372017ccf930"],
 ", not of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], "4"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "b8194cfb-f4fb-4ed4-805f-8de7bc8f910f"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e4d5c85-65a6-4845-842e-e443b9e9e13e"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"quotient", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"NondegenerateQuotient", "[", "bad", "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"quotient", "[", "\"\<Basis\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"quotient", "[", "\"\<Differential\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
    RowBox[{"Values", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"HodgeTypeReport", "[", "bad", "]"}], "[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "\"\<Cohomology\>\""}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",ExpressionUUID->"3e8df321-a69b-45d0-bd29-bc732164f6a5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "a", ",", 
     SuperscriptBox["a", "2"]}], "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", "2"}], 
  "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[8]= ",ExpressionUUID->"ea2e6f39-c689-4760-8a39-4339c9238702"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Three against two: the quotient map has killed the class of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "8ea60be3-9155-4d26-a995-df54fbda29bb"],
 " but not the class ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"[", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "]"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "af221102-ed1f-4362-b640-69a17c882f8c"],
 " that ought to have died with it. The repair in the reference is to ",
 StyleBox["extend", "TI"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["V", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3f04b338-de33-4b18-aa5c-961a436b9f0a"],
 " to a larger PDGA of Hodge type that retracts onto it; the extension \
adjoins a generator in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "e454d62d-439c-49fb-abd8-5215b2c7a735"],
 ", which is why this example also shows that no ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "9dd725bd-3c3c-46db-a419-0211e0517ede"],
 "-connected extension of Hodge type exists in degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["4", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "05c2f229-a326-448f-a2fb-164b19a6b6c4"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e19a88b0-393c-4c8d-b1ac-3d1c1de65dce"],

Cell["When the model is already a dPD algebra", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"39d1f33c-e5c7-461c-8c05-3e4ae77b51d1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At the other extreme are models whose pairing is already perfect on chain \
level, so ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["deg",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6906d861-92ea-475d-9f70-e31cad69f794"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["Q", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["V", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f047f281-f977-4a8e-8d1e-7257f85168bb"],
 ". The minimal model of a nilmanifold is one: a finite-dimensional exterior \
algebra on generators of degree ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "83fc5a53-c398-4c6d-aa05-929b29414985"],
 ", with the differential of the nilpotent Lie algebra."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0502f235-1452-41f9-811c-530e8b034b88"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The three-dimensional Heisenberg nilmanifold has ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[CapitalLambda]", "(", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["x", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["y", "TI"], ",", 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "f56b452b-ca11-40e8-ad70-a4ecf037b557"],
 " with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
    StyleBox["x", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["y", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1aefdd83-d66e-4d07-9b58-ba18c3a52ecc"],
 ", and the orientation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["1", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c2b4119a-177f-40f9-b781-5ca0040ff378"],
 " on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"x", "y", "z"}], "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76a6f57b-83da-4b53-b975-86888ab43761"],
 "."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0293fc30-984b-4fa3-8e0f-e9d4c72401c9"],

